PartialFillSettler_finaliseAsRefunded
├── when _hashOrder(order) is not equal to orderDigest
│   └── it should revert with DigestMismatch
├── when block.timestamp is at or before order.fillDeadline
│   └── it should revert with NotExpired
├── when orderStatus[orderId] is not Opened
│   └── it should revert with InvalidOrderStatus
├── when UW's ERC-1271 smart-wallet policy changed post-signing
│   └── it should succeed without signature re-verification (liveness)
├── when for a given filler f.premiumSettled is true
│   └── it should skip (route via finaliseAsSettled)
├── when for a given filler f.dstCstProduced is zero
│   └── it should skip (no rollover-leg)
├── when for a given filler f.refunded is already true
│   └── it should skip idempotently
├── when for a given filler f.finalised is true
│   └── it should skip (exclusive paths)
├── for each eligible filler
│   └── it should set f.refunded to true BEFORE any external call, increment refundedCount, decrement totalDstCstEscrowed, dstCST.safeTransfer f.dstCstProduced to cellar, and emit FillerRefunded
├── when refundedCount equals participantCount after the loop
│   └── it should transition orderStatus from Opened to Refunded and emit OrderFinalised with status Refunded
├── when refundedCount is less than participantCount after the loop
│   └── it should leave orderStatus as Opened
├── when entire fillers[] is premium-paid
│   └── it should transfer zero tokens (all skip)
└── when called by any caller AND status is Opened
    └── it should succeed (permissionless keeper-friendly)
